1
00:00:43,470 --> 00:00:44,240
What?

2
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:47,900
Yesterday, it's sunny.

3
00:00:47,900 --> 00:00:49,740
Now, it's a WINDSTORM!

4
00:00:49,740 --> 00:00:51,470
How did THAT happen?

5
00:00:52,080 --> 00:00:53,550
Hold on a second.

6
00:00:53,640 --> 00:00:57,600
This all happened because of
your cake, didn't it Needy?!

7
00:00:58,300 --> 00:00:59,600
Don't call me Needy!

8
00:00:59,690 --> 00:01:00,970
LEAFY:
Calm DOWN!

9
00:01:01,230 --> 00:01:03,500
What's wrong with calling you Needy, Needy?

10
00:01:04,030 --> 00:01:07,580
Oh, so you want a slap fight now, don't you, Needy!?

11
00:01:08,030 --> 00:01:10,200
Well, I can slap, TOO!

12
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:13,610
Uh-oh!

13
00:01:13,840 --> 00:01:15,520
SNOWBALL:
She deserved it!

14
00:01:15,520 --> 00:01:17,240
It was HER cake!

15
00:01:24,200 --> 00:01:25,230
AHH!

16
00:01:26,190 --> 00:01:33,050
♪ [INTRO PLAYS] ♪

17
00:01:33,050 --> 00:01:35,050
Subtitles: Daniel Adam Valle

18
00:01:35,770 --> 00:01:37,290
Gloop-gloop, doot-doot.

19
00:01:37,580 --> 00:01:40,270
It's time for Cake at Stake for the Cherries.

20
00:01:40,560 --> 00:01:41,360
♪ Da-da-da-da-da-da ♪

21
00:01:41,360 --> 00:01:42,880
♪ Cake at Stake! ♪

22
00:01:43,100 --> 00:01:44,400
There's eight of you now.

23
00:01:44,810 --> 00:01:46,430
There will only be seven later.

24
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:50,460
Okay, so we got fourteen votes.

25
00:01:50,880 --> 00:01:54,680
Well, I wanted to make an ice cream
cake, but I forgot the ice cream.

26
00:01:54,680 --> 00:01:56,680
So I made a chunk of ice again.

27
00:01:56,680 --> 00:01:58,220
NOOO!

28
00:01:58,220 --> 00:01:59,040
BLAAAH!

29
00:01:59,070 --> 00:02:01,710
OMPF! Overreacting!

30
00:02:01,900 --> 00:02:04,430
JK! I have an ice cream cake.

31
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,790
If you get no cake, you leave BF Dream Island.

32
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:11,180
Pin, you have a Win Token.
Would you like to use it now?

33
00:02:11,180 --> 00:02:12,410
Uh, no.

34
00:02:12,760 --> 00:02:14,040
I mean there's nothing mean I-

35
00:02:14,040 --> 00:02:15,420
Yeah, yeah, we know.

36
00:02:15,710 --> 00:02:17,340
Bubble is at zero votes...

37
00:02:17,340 --> 00:02:18,460
[DEEP VOICE]
AGAIN.

38
00:02:23,930 --> 00:02:26,330
Ew, gross! A needle!

39
00:02:26,330 --> 00:02:28,830
OMG! You don't like 'em?

40
00:02:28,830 --> 00:02:30,830
I love Needies!

41
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:34,200
Don't slap me! I said, "NEEDLE"!

42
00:02:34,330 --> 00:02:36,540
Now, I will say who else has zero votes.

43
00:02:37,070 --> 00:02:38,140
Pen,

44
00:02:38,140 --> 00:02:39,180
Pencil,

45
00:02:39,180 --> 00:02:40,330
and Firey.

46
00:02:41,980 --> 00:02:43,690
Hey! No fair!

47
00:02:45,480 --> 00:02:47,340
Hey, where's my cake!?

48
00:02:47,390 --> 00:02:49,130
Oh, oh, yeah, I forgot.

49
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:52,380
Hey!

50
00:02:54,090 --> 00:02:58,410
Grr! I'm gonna crush you, Announcer Speaker thing!

51
00:02:59,020 --> 00:03:01,020
Needle, what are you doing here?

52
00:03:01,020 --> 00:03:02,380
You're on the other team.

53
00:03:02,380 --> 00:03:03,980
Aw, seriously?

54
00:03:04,430 --> 00:03:06,490
ANNOUNCER:
You four all got at least one vote.

55
00:03:06,880 --> 00:03:09,600
Match and Eraser, you both got one vote, a pie-

56
00:03:09,600 --> 00:03:11,600
I mean you both got one vote each.

57
00:03:11,600 --> 00:03:12,430
Thank you!

58
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:16,300
- ANNOUNCER: Woody...
- WOODY: Ahh...

59
00:03:16,300 --> 00:03:17,850
...is eliminated at nine votes.

60
00:03:17,850 --> 00:03:19,850
HEAAAUUUGHUEAAAOOOH!

61
00:03:19,850 --> 00:03:23,640
Sorry, Woody. You didn't not ain't
not get no any none of nothing.

62
00:03:23,640 --> 00:03:25,640
Let's fling him to the TLC!

63
00:03:25,640 --> 00:03:29,500
Wait, you always say "the TLC".

64
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:31,070
Is it an object?

65
00:03:31,070 --> 00:03:32,990
You mean the Tiny Loser Chamber?

66
00:03:32,990 --> 00:03:34,990
Duh! Of course it's an object.

67
00:03:34,990 --> 00:03:37,450
WOODY:
HEEEAAAEEEAAAEEE!

68
00:03:40,560 --> 00:03:42,760
FLOWER:
Uh-oh, It's CLOSING!

69
00:03:42,760 --> 00:03:47,230
BLOCKY: Awh, why do we get only
five minutes of sunlight a day?

70
00:03:47,230 --> 00:03:49,230
FLOWER:
Move over, Blocky!

71
00:04:02,010 --> 00:04:03,230
I don't know about you,

72
00:04:03,230 --> 00:04:05,880
Need-ULLLAAH,

73
00:04:06,360 --> 00:04:08,750
but that bridge doesn't look so strong.

74
00:04:08,860 --> 00:04:11,610
And I can't see the bottom of that gorge!

75
00:04:23,310 --> 00:04:24,570
Go, Bubble!

76
00:04:24,570 --> 00:04:26,570
Woi-huh-hoi-huh! Hey!

77
00:04:26,750 --> 00:04:28,090
Yeah, SB!

78
00:04:28,090 --> 00:04:31,760
Can you believe he didn't even try my cake?

79
00:04:32,430 --> 00:04:34,240
You know, that's really mean...

80
00:04:34,240 --> 00:04:36,720
Your tiny, teeny-tiny little brain...

81
00:04:36,720 --> 00:04:43,530
[GOLF BALL GIBBERISH]

82
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:45,920
...I mean, I just don't understand!

83
00:04:45,920 --> 00:04:47,790
Hold on, Coiny!

84
00:04:47,790 --> 00:04:50,720
I've got some BUSINESS to take care of!

85
00:04:51,470 --> 00:04:52,510
GB!

86
00:04:52,730 --> 00:04:55,180
It's time to PAY!

87
00:04:55,400 --> 00:04:56,760
HEUUGH!

88
00:04:57,680 --> 00:05:00,010
Do do-do do, do do-do!

89
00:05:00,460 --> 00:05:01,560
Oh! Oh, no!

90
00:05:01,560 --> 00:05:02,800
Oh, no!

91
00:05:03,080 --> 00:05:03,880
OEAAAH!

92
00:05:03,880 --> 00:05:05,470
Bubble, gotcha!

93
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:08,540
I'm in an alliance! We have to stick TOGETHER!

94
00:05:09,370 --> 00:05:12,780
Great! How do we cross without a bridge?

95
00:05:12,780 --> 00:05:14,760
There's another one down there!

96
00:05:14,760 --> 00:05:15,560
ERASER:
Oh.

97
00:05:15,610 --> 00:05:19,240
Icy, do you still want revenge?

98
00:05:19,610 --> 00:05:20,760
How's this?

99
00:05:20,840 --> 00:05:22,990
I'll help you cross the bridge!

100
00:05:23,360 --> 00:05:24,970
Needle, you, too!

101
00:05:24,970 --> 00:05:26,780
Let's all go TOGETHER!

102
00:05:27,130 --> 00:05:28,160
GOTCHA!

103
00:05:28,480 --> 00:05:32,380
WAAAOOOAAOOOAAAAAOOUU!

104
00:05:34,430 --> 00:05:36,760
Now, THAT was totally uncalled for.

105
00:05:36,760 --> 00:05:39,080
You wanna go down there, too?!

106
00:05:39,080 --> 00:05:41,580
Please, Snowball. Calm down.

107
00:05:41,580 --> 00:05:43,040
THAT'S IT!

108
00:05:44,040 --> 00:05:45,240
HOLD ON!

109
00:05:45,240 --> 00:05:47,680
These dumb sticks are in the way!

110
00:05:50,360 --> 00:05:51,870
Seriously?!

111
00:05:52,320 --> 00:05:55,470
Pen, see any third bridge?

112
00:05:55,470 --> 00:05:59,740
No, but the old bridge still has its rope railings.

113
00:05:59,740 --> 00:06:01,870
We can climb down those!

114
00:06:01,870 --> 00:06:04,990
ERASER:
There is no way I am doing that!

115
00:06:04,990 --> 00:06:08,620
But don't you want to win and get Dream Island?

116
00:06:08,620 --> 00:06:13,000
I DO! When I win, there will be
a big sign in front saying...

117
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:16,000
"PENISLAND", no spaces, all caps!

118
00:06:16,280 --> 00:06:18,000
So let's do this!

119
00:06:18,350 --> 00:06:22,120
Snowball, you're not gonna throw me off, are you?

120
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:25,370
No, Coiny. You're my friend!

121
00:06:25,370 --> 00:06:27,020
What about Teardrop?

122
00:06:27,020 --> 00:06:30,990
Well, as long as she doesn't say I'm bad...

123
00:06:30,990 --> 00:06:33,240
SB? She can't talk.

124
00:06:33,760 --> 00:06:37,230
Okay, Pen. You go first.

125
00:06:37,230 --> 00:06:38,240
Ooh! Ah! Oh! Ah!

126
00:06:38,240 --> 00:06:39,920
Hold on a second.

127
00:06:39,920 --> 00:06:44,040
These are just black bendy straws attached with tape!

128
00:06:44,240 --> 00:06:45,800
Wait, WHAT?!

129
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:47,950
AAAAAHHHHH!

130
00:06:47,950 --> 00:06:49,160
Hold it! Hold it!

131
00:06:49,160 --> 00:06:53,920
Since none of you crossed the bridge, and there
is no way the remaining six of you can cross,

132
00:06:53,920 --> 00:06:57,450
it's a tie, zero to zero. So we need a tiebreaker.

133
00:06:57,450 --> 00:07:01,340
Whichever team manages to rip their
team necktie first wins the contest.

134
00:07:01,340 --> 00:07:02,440
Get it? Tie Breaker?

135
00:07:02,830 --> 00:07:05,800
The Squashy Grapes win, so
one of the Cherries goes home.

136
00:07:05,900 --> 00:07:07,880
There are seven Cherries to choose from.

137
00:07:08,160 --> 00:07:10,010
Go ahead. Vote one off.

138
00:07:14,730 --> 00:07:16,760
Hey, where's Golf Ball?

139
00:07:17,020 --> 00:07:18,700
I thought she fell, too!

140
00:07:18,700 --> 00:07:20,280
PEN:
Um, Match?

141
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:22,750
Golf balls... sink.

142
00:07:22,750 --> 00:07:24,560
So do rocks.